{"id":"mahabharata-3-265","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":265,"title":"पञ्चषष्ट्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 265 · Sita rejects Ravana","summary":{"en":"Ravana comes to the grieving Sita and woos her with promises of wealth and power. Sita, placing a blade of grass between them, rejects him with scorn, declaring her loyalty to Rama, and Ravana departs, leaving her among the Rakshasis.","kn":"ರಾವಣನು ದುಃಖಿತ ಸೀತೆಯ ಬಳಿ ಬಂದು ಸಂಪತ್ತು ಅಧಿಕಾರಗಳ ಭರವಸೆಯೊಂದಿಗೆ ಅವಳನ್ನು ಒಲಿಸಲು ಯತ್ನಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ನಡುವೆ ಹುಲ್ಲುಕಡ್ಡಿಯನ್ನಿಟ್ಟು ಸೀತೆ ತಿರಸ್ಕಾರದಿಂದ ಅವನನ್ನು ನಿರಾಕರಿಸಿ ಶ್ರೀರಾಮನಿಗೆ ತನ್ನ ನಿಷ್ಠೆಯನ್ನು ಘೋಷಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ; ರಾವಣನು ಅವಳನ್ನು ರಾಕ್ಷಸಿಯರ ನಡುವೆ ಬಿಟ್ಟು ತೆರಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"रावण शोकाकुल सीता के पास आकर धन और शक्ति के वचनों से उन्हें लुभाता है। सीता बीच में एक तिनका रखकर तिरस्कार से उसे ठुकराती हैं और श्रीराम के प्रति अपनी निष्ठा की घोषणा करती हैं, और रावण उन्हें राक्षसियों के बीच छोड़कर चला जाता है।","te":"రావణుడు దుఃఖంలో ఉన్న సీత దగ్గరకు వచ్చి సంపద, అధికారాల వాగ్దానాలతో ఆమెను లోబరచుకోవాలని ప్రయత్నిస్తాడు. మధ్యలో గడ్డిపోచ ఉంచి సీత తిరస్కారంతో అతనిని నిరాకరించి శ్రీరామునిపై తన నిష్ఠను ప్రకటిస్తుంది; రావణుడు ఆమెను రాక్షసస్త్రీల మధ్య వదిలి వెళ్తాడు.","ta":"ராவணன் துயருற்ற ஸீதையிடம் வந்து செல்வமும் அதிகாரமும் தருவதாக வாக்களித்து அவளை வசப்படுத்த முயல்கிறான். இடையில் ஒரு புல்லை வைத்து ஸீதை இகழ்ச்சியுடன் அவனை மறுத்து ஸ்ரீராமர் மீதான தன் பற்றை அறிவிக்க, ராவணன் அவளை அரக்கியரிடையே விட்டுச் செல்கிறான்.","ml":"ദുഃഖിതയായ സീതയുടെ അടുത്തെത്തി രാവണൻ സമ്പത്തും അധികാരവും വാഗ്ദാനം ചെയ്ത് അവളെ മോഹിപ്പിക്കുന്നു. തങ്ങൾക്കിടയിൽ ഒരു പുൽനാമ്പ് വെച്ച് സീത പുച്ഛത്തോടെ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ തിരസ്കരിക്കുന്നു, രാമനോടുള്ള തന്റെ വിശ്വസ്തത പ്രഖ്യാപിക്കുന്നു; രാവണൻ അവളെ രാക്ഷസിമാരുടെ ഇടയിൽ വിട്ട് പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.265; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"द्रौपदीहरणपर्व","titleEn":"Draupadiharana Parva (Abduction of Draupadi)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततस्तां भर्तृशोकार्तां दीनां मलिनवाससम् ।\nमणिशेषाभ्यलंकारां रुदतीं च पतिव्रताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Ravana, struck by the arrows of love, saw her, miserable and grieving for her husband, in dirty clothes, with only a few jewels left, weeping, a faithful wife,"}},{"n":2,"text":"राक्षसीभिरुपास्यन्तीं समासीनां शिलातले ।\nरावणः कामबाणार्तो ददर्शोपससर्प च ॥","meaning":{"en":"seated on a rock slab, attended by rakshasis, and he approached her."}},{"n":3,"text":"देवदानवगन्धर्वयक्षकिंपुरुषैर्युधि ।\nअजितोऽशोकवनिकां ययौ कन्दर्पमोहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ravana, whom gods, danavas, gandharvas, yakshas, and kimpurushas had not conquered in battle, went to the Ashoka grove, bewildered by passion."}},{"n":4,"text":"दिव्याम्बरधरः श्रीमान्सुमृष्टमणिकुण्डलः ।\nविचित्रमाल्यमुकुटो वसन्त इव मूर्तिमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He wore divine garments and bright polished jeweled earrings, with a crown of varied garlands, looking like Spring in person."}},{"n":5,"text":"स कल्पवृक्षसदृशो यत्नादपि विभूषितः ।\nश्मशानचैत्यद्रुमवद्भूषितोऽपि भयंकरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was like a wishing tree in splendor, carefully adorned, yet frightening, like a cemetery tree adorned with decorations."}},{"n":6,"text":"स तस्यास्तनुमध्यायाः समीपे रजनीचरः ।\nददृशे रोहिणीमेत्य शनैश्चर इव ग्रहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That night-wanderer appeared beside the slender-waisted woman as the planet Saturn appears near Rohini."}},{"n":7,"text":"स तामामन्त्र्य सुश्रोणीं पुष्पकेतुशराहतः ।\nइदमित्यब्रवीद्बालां त्रस्तां रौहीमिवाबलाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by the flower-bannered god's arrows, he addressed the lovely-hipped girl, trembling like a frightened doe, and said:"}},{"n":8,"text":"सीते पर्याप्तमेतावत्कृतो भर्तुरनुग्रहः ।\nप्रसादं कुरु तन्वङ्गि क्रियतां परिकर्म ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Sita, you have been favored enough in being faithful to your husband. Show me your grace, slender one, and let me have you attended to."}},{"n":9,"text":"भजस्व मां वरारोहे महार्हाभरणाम्बरा ।\nभव मे सर्वनारीणामुत्तमा वरवर्णिनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Come to me, fair woman; dressed in precious ornaments and robes, be the foremost of all my women, bright-complexioned one."}},{"n":10,"text":"सन्ति मे देवकन्याश्च राजर्षीणां तथाङ्गनाः ।\nसन्ति दानवकन्याश्च दैत्यानां चापि योषितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have daughters of gods and wives of royal sages; I have daughters of danavas and women of the daityas."}},{"n":11,"text":"चतुर्दश पिशाचानां कोट्यो मे वचने स्थिताः ।\nद्विस्तावत्पुरुषादानां रक्षसां भीमकर्मणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fourteen crores of pishachis stand at my command, and twice as many fierce man-eating rakshasas."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततो मे त्रिगुणा यक्षा ये मद्वचनकारिणः ।\nकेचिदेव धनाध्यक्षं भ्रातरं मे समाश्रिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Three times that number are yakshas who obey me, and some have taken refuge with my brother, the lord of wealth."}},{"n":13,"text":"गन्धर्वाप्सरसो भद्रे मामापानगतं सदा ।\nउपतिष्ठन्ति वामोरु यथैव भ्रातरं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gandharvas and apsarases attend me always when I am at my drink, fair woman, just as they attend my brother."}},{"n":14,"text":"पुत्रोऽहमपि विप्रर्षेः साक्षाद्विश्रवसो मुनेः ।\nपञ्चमो लोकपालानामिति मे प्रथितं यशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I too am the son of the Brahmin sage Vishravas himself, and my fame is that I am the fifth of the world-guardians."}},{"n":15,"text":"दिव्यानि भक्ष्यभोज्यानि पानानि विविधानि च ।\nयथैव त्रिदशेशस्य तथैव मम भामिनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Heavenly foods and drinks of many kinds are mine, just as they are the lord of the gods'."}},{"n":16,"text":"क्षीयतां दुष्कृतं कर्म वनवासकृतं तव ।\nभार्या मे भव सुश्रोणि यथा मन्दोदरी तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let the evil you earned by living in the forest be wiped out. Be my wife, fair-hipped one, as Mandodari is.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"इत्युक्ता तेन वैदेही परिवृत्य शुभानना ।\nतृणमन्तरतः कृत्वा तमुवाच निशाचरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, Sita, fair-faced, turned aside, placed a blade of grass between them, and spoke to the night-wanderer."}},{"n":18,"text":"अशिवेनातिवामोरूरजस्रं नेत्रवारिणा ।\nस्तनावपतितौ बाला सहितावभिवर्षती ।\nउवाच वाक्यं तं क्षुद्रं वैदेही पतिदेवता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Her lovely thighs and the breasts that she had were wet with the ceaseless tears of misfortune as she, devoted to her husband as to a god, answered that petty creature."}},{"n":19,"text":"असकृद्वदतो वाक्यमीदृशं राक्षसेश्वर ।\nविषादयुक्तमेतत्ते मया श्रुतमभाग्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Lord of the rakshasas, I have heard you say such things again and again, speech full of grief for you, and I am unlucky to hear it."}},{"n":20,"text":"तद्भद्रसुख भद्रं ते मानसं विनिवर्त्यताम् ।\nपरदारास्म्यलभ्या च सततं च पतिव्रता ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, blessed one, turn your mind away; I am another man's wife, not to be won, and always faithful to my husband."}},{"n":21,"text":"न चैवोपयिकी भार्या मानुषी कृपणा तव ।\nविवशां धर्षयित्वा च कां त्वं प्रीतिमवाप्स्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"I, a human wretch, am not a fit wife for you; by forcing a helpless woman, what joy will you gain?"}},{"n":22,"text":"प्रजापतिसमो विप्रो ब्रह्मयोनिः पिता तव ।\nन च पालयसे धर्मं लोकपालसमः कथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your father is a Brahmin like Prajapati, born of Brahma. How, being equal to a world-guardian, do you not uphold dharma?"}},{"n":23,"text":"भ्रातरं राजराजानं महेश्वरसखं प्रभुम् ।\nधनेश्वरं व्यपदिशन्कथं त्विह न लज्जसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Naming your brother Kubera, king of kings, friend of Mahadeva, how are you not ashamed?\""}},{"n":24,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा प्रारुदत्सीता कम्पयन्ती पयोधरौ ।\nशिरोधरां च तन्वङ्गी मुखं प्रच्छाद्य वाससा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, Sita wept, her breasts and neck trembling, her face covered with her cloth."}},{"n":25,"text":"तस्या रुदत्या भामिन्या दीर्घा वेणी सुसंयता ।\nददृशे स्वसिता स्निग्धा काली व्यालीव मूर्धनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"As she wept, the lovely woman's long, tightly bound braid looked like a glossy black snake on her head."}},{"n":26,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा रावणो वाक्यं सीतयोक्तं सुनिष्ठुरम् ।\nप्रत्याख्यातोऽपि दुर्मेधाः पुनरेवाब्रवीद्वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Sita's very harsh words, Ravana, though rejected, spoke again, dull-witted as he was."}},{"n":27,"text":"काममङ्गानि मे सीते दुनोतु मकरध्वजः ।\nन त्वामकामां सुश्रोणीं समेष्ये चारुहासिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let the god of love torment my limbs as he wills, Sita, but I will not approach you against your wish, fair-hipped, sweet-smiling one."}},{"n":28,"text":"किं नु शक्यं मया कर्तुं यत्त्वमद्यापि मानुषम् ।\nआहारभूतमस्माकं राममेवानुरुध्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"What can I do, that even now you cling to Rama, a mere man, our food?\""}},{"n":29,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा तामनिन्द्याङ्गीं स राक्षसगणेश्वरः ।\nतत्रैवान्तर्हितो भूत्वा जगामाभिमतां दिशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this to the faultless woman, that lord of the rakshasa hosts vanished on the spot and went to the place he wished."}},{"n":30,"text":"राक्षसीभिः परिवृता वैदेही शोककर्शिता ।\nसेव्यमाना त्रिजटया तत्रैव न्यवसत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded by rakshasis, wasted by grief, Sita lived there, attended by Trijata."}}]}]}